  "id": "COMPOUND:26933 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex network of interactions between 2-Methoxyjuglone and SF-188, mediated through multiple targets. The drug 2-Methoxyjuglone is identified as a target of several enzymes, including Dehydrogenase/reductase SDR family member 9 and Lysine-specific demethylase 4D-like, which in turn target compounds such as 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol and 23-Hydroxy-3-Oxoolean-12-En-27-Oic Acid. These intermediates ultimately have SF-188 as their target. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism where 2-Methoxyjuglone may influence SF-188 through the modulation of these enzymatic activities, possibly by altering the metabolic pathways that lead to the formation of SF-188. The evidence suggests a dependency on these enzymatic targets, but the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear, necessitating further investigation into the specific molecular mechanisms involved.",
